{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8e2b6a4c-1d3f-4a2b-9c7e-visualregression01",
    "name": "Visual Regression API",
    "description": "Covers every endpoint under /api/v1 for the Visual Regression tool (server/src/routes), with one request per test case mirrored from the Jest integration suite (server/tests/integration/*.test.ts) plus additional negative-path cases (invalid file type, not-found, expired report).\n\n**Setup**\n1. Start the server: `cd server && npm run dev` (listens on PORT from server/.env, default 4000).\n2. Select the \"Visual Regression - Local\" environment.\n3. Run folders top-to-bottom — Comparisons requests populate `comparisonId_*` environment variables that the Reports folder consumes.\n\n**Fixtures** — file-upload requests point at real files already in this repo so they work out of the box on this machine:\n- `Dashboard.png` / `Dashboard New.png` (project root) as baseline/current screenshots.\n- `postman/fixtures/invalid-file.txt` for the invalid-file-type case.\nIf you move this collection to another machine, re-point those form-data file fields at local images.\n\n**⚠️ Settings folder caution** — `PATCH /settings` persists changes straight to `server/.env` (see `src/lib/runtimeConfig.ts` / `envFile.ts`). Every request in that folder that mutates a value restores it immediately afterward using the real values found in this project's `server/.env` at collection-build time. Two requests are marked destructive because they touch API-key fields and are left disabled by default — read their descriptions before enabling them.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
